# Backend Summary - Portfolio CMS

This document provides a detailed overview of the backend architecture, file structure, and API endpoints for the Portfolio CMS.

## 📁 File Structure

The backend is built with **Django** and **Django REST Framework (DRF)**.

```text
backend/
├── manage.py              # Django CLI entry point
├── requirements.txt       # Project dependencies
├── config/                # Core configuration directory
│   ├── settings.py        # Main project settings (DB, JWT, Apps)
│   ├── urls.py            # Root URL routing
│   ├── permissions.py     # Custom IsAdminOrReadOnly permission
│   ├── asgi.py            # ASGI entry point for production
│   └── wsgi.py            # WSGI entry point for production
├── accounts/              # Authentication & User management
│   ├── urls.py            # JWT (Login/Refresh) routes
│   └── ...                # Standard Django app files
├── projects/              # Portfolio Projects
│   ├── models.py          # Project model with slug auto-generation
│   ├── serializers.py     # DRF serializers for Project model
│   ├── views.py           # ModelViewSet for Project CRUD
│   └── urls.py            # Router-based URL patterns
├── blogs/                 # Blog management
│   ├── models.py          # Blog model (title, content, tags, published status)
│   ├── serializers.py     # DRF serializers for Blog model
│   ├── views.py           # Logic to filter published posts for public
│   └── urls.py            # Router-based URL patterns
├── experience/            # Professional Experience
│   ├── models.py          # Experience model (role, organization, duration)
│   ├── serializers.py     # DRF serializers
│   └── views.py           # CRUD views
├── skills/                # Technical Skills
│   ├── models.py          # Skill model (name, category)
│   ├── serializers.py     # DRF serializers
│   └── views.py           # CRUD views
├── contact/               # Contact Form Submissions
│   ├── models.py          # ContactMessage model
│   ├── serializers.py     # DRF serializers
│   └── views.py           # Permissions: Anyone can POST, Admin can GET/DELETE
└── resume/                # Resume/CV Management
    ├── models.py          # Resume model (only one active at a time)
    ├── serializers.py     # DRF serializers
    └── views.py           # CRUD + /current/ endpoint for active resume
```

